From 14428533c94bbb8cc6589731b7df214f6b43cff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 17:40:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 57/59] rescue: run console commands from the web page
 (task-97)

Expose the shared console slot to the rescue page the way the upstream
failsafe does, without building an HTTP-to-telnet bridge:

  - POST /console/exec takes a multipart body with the cmd field (and
    the optional token field when failsafe_console_token is set), runs
    run_command() from the poll loop and answers JSON.
  - POST /console/poll returns the console record bytes as JSON, with
    avail, overflow and busy; POST /console/abort requests the same
    mtk_tcp_abort_request() the telnet server uses, and POST
    /console/clear resets the record ring.
  - The web console and telnetd share one execution slot: either side
    answers 503 / "console is busy" while the other runs, and the TCP
    server keeps its weak busy hook overridden by the rescue.
  - After a network command the rescue loop re-inits eth outside the TCP
    callback chain and re-registers the DHCP and DNS handlers.
  - The header helpers for multipart parsing and JSON escaping live in
    e2631webconsole.h so a host fixture can exercise them.

The multipart helpers, the JSON escape and the command-field path are
covered by uboot-port/tests/webconsole_test.c.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
